&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong grasp of web application security principles&lt;/strong&gt; and hands-on experience with application testing tools (Burp Suite, OWASP ZAP, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Software development experience building security tools&lt;/strong&gt; in at least one modern language (Go, Python, Java/Kotlin, TypeScript, Ruby, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Track record of leading multi-team technical initiatives&lt;/strong&gt; and mentoring engineers into senior roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running or scaling a security champions program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identity management and identity federation experience (SAML, OAuth, SCIM)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with IaaS cloud infrastructure, Kubernetes, containers, and service-oriented architectures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with bug bounty platforms and SAST tools (Cycode, Semgrep, Snyk, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience performing code audits on internal or open-source libraries before they ship in production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;How We Work&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We stay closely aligned with teammates on other continents via Slack, video, and async docs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We have the latest hardware and software, including frontier AI models on day one&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We&#39;re agile, but not dogmatic — the team decides how it works best&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why This Role Is Special&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Massive leverage: the conventions and champions program you build are multiplied across hundreds of engineers who never talk to you directly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Broad authority: you set the architecture other reviews are measured against, rather than being the one measured.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re part of PSI: the platform, security, and infrastructure teams work hand in hand, and security is treated as infrastructure with real engineering quality bars, not a policy function.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
